From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 09:31:24 +0200
Subject: leds: lgm-sso: write the blink fields at their own width

sso_led_freq_set() treats the blink rate and the clock-source select as
three-bit fields and writes them one field too high. For a field whose
low bit sits at low it takes high = low + 2, masks with
GENMASK(high, low), and shifts the value by high.

Those fields are two bits wide. A LED_BLINK_H8_* register gives each
blink slot six bits -- an FPID rank, a GPTC rank, and the select that
says which of the two the hardware reads -- which is what
GET_FREQ_OFFSET()'s (src * 2) stride and GET_SRC_OFFSET()'s + 4 already
describe. low + 2 is therefore not the top of the field but the bottom
of the next one. So the value lands entirely in that neighbour, while
the mask spans the whole intended field plus the neighbour's bottom
bit: the update clears the field it set out to write, and the only bit
it can set belongs to somebody else.

The clock-source select is where this is felt. It is written last, and
it is what decides whether the hardware reads the pin's FPID rank or
its GPTC rank; left as found, a device tree asking for one of the four
GPTC-derived rates gets the FPID source the register came up with. The
rate does not arrive either, because the rank write missed in the same
way. And since the neighbouring slot belongs to another pin, asking one
LED for a blink rate disturbs the next one's -- or, for the last slot
of LED_BLINK_H8_0, shifts past the last bit the register implements and
is dropped on the floor.

Mask and shift at the field's own width. The vendor driver this one was
rewritten from writes both fields as (val & 0x3) << off.

Pins 0..23 are unaffected: sso_led_freq_set() returns early for them.
No device tree in tree declares a pin in either of the upper two
groups, which is how this survived alongside the rest.

Fixes: c3987cd2bca3 ("leds: lgm: Add LED controller driver for LGM SoC")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/drivers/leds/blink/leds-lgm-sso.c b/drivers/leds/blink/leds-lgm-sso.c
index 9644a8433226..720955112b11 100644
--- a/drivers/leds/blink/leds-lgm-sso.c
+++ b/drivers/leds/blink/leds-lgm-sso.c
@@ -24,6 +24,12 @@
 
 #define LED_BLINK_H8_0			0x0
 #define LED_BLINK_H8_1			0x4
+/*
+ * A LED_BLINK_H8_* register gives every blink slot six bits, as three two-bit
+ * fields: the FPID rank, then the GPTC rank, then the select that says which
+ * of the two the hardware reads. Pins 24..31 get a slot each; pins 0..23 share
+ * the one sso_led_pin_blink_off() calls the "led 32 location".
+ */
 #define GET_FREQ_OFFSET(pin, src)	(((pin) * 6) + ((src) * 2))
 #define GET_SRC_OFFSET(pinc)		(((pinc) * 6) + 4)
 
@@ -206,7 +212,7 @@ static struct sso_led
 static void sso_led_freq_set(struct sso_led_priv *priv, u32 pin, int freq_idx)
 {
 	u32 reg, off, freq_src, val_freq;
-	u32 low, high, val;
+	u32 low, val;
 	unsigned int group;
 
 	if (!freq_idx)
@@ -231,16 +237,14 @@ static void sso_led_freq_set(struct sso_led_priv *priv, u32 pin, int freq_idx)
 	/* set blink rate idx */
 	if (freq_src != CLK_SRC_GPTC_HS) {
 		low = GET_FREQ_OFFSET(off, freq_src);
-		high = low + 2;
-		val = val_freq << high;
-		regmap_update_bits(priv->mmap, reg, GENMASK(high, low), val);
+		val = val_freq << low;
+		regmap_update_bits(priv->mmap, reg, GENMASK(low + 1, low), val);
 	}
 
 	/* select clock source */
 	low = GET_SRC_OFFSET(off);
-	high = low + 2;
-	val = freq_src << high;
-	regmap_update_bits(priv->mmap, reg, GENMASK(high, low), val);
+	val = freq_src << low;
+	regmap_update_bits(priv->mmap, reg, GENMASK(low + 1, low), val);
 }
 
